{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For the sons of Joseph, for Ephraim.</b> After he mentioned the sons of Leah first, he mentioned the sons of Joseph, and he mentioned Ephraim before Manasseh, for so did Jacob their father do, as it says (Genesis 48:20): ״וישם את אפרים לפני מנשה״. And afterward he mentioned the sons of Benjamin, and for the honor of Rachel he placed them before the sons of the maidservants. And afterward he mentioned the sons of the maidservants, and he began with Dan, who is the firstborn of the maidservants, and he joined to him Asher, who encamps at the head alongside the standard of Dan, as it says (Numbers 2:27): ״והחונים עליו מטה אשר״, because he is joined to him to illuminate his darkness. And afterward he mentioned Gad, who is the firstborn of Leah's maidservant, and he joined to him Naphtali."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:32.564014057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}